<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beiyang government</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beiyang government was the internationally recognised government of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> seated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> from 1912 to 1928, dominated by officers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-army">Beiyang Army</a> built up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a> under the Qing. After Yuan's death in 1916 rival cliques of warlords fought for control of it. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a> ended it in 1928.</p></div>
